# Live suites against the isolated clean-room environment, 2026-10-06 (synthetic data)

Run: `python3 scripts/deploy_snowflake.py --profile cleanroom --suffix <SUFFIX> --apply --step test`, as the owner role and then as the application role, on the redeployed app
(30 of 30 code files byte-identical to the source) with the saved responses and the 19-alert seed.

RESULT, as run: owner role 18 passed, 1 skipped, **1 failed**; application role 17 passed, 1 skipped, 1 deselected, **1 failed**.
The one failure in each role is `test_alerts_and_transactions_seeded`: it still asserted the label counts and the alert count of the earlier 16-alert seed (FILE 9, NOT_FILE 3; 16 alerts).
That was a stale constant in the test, not a behaviour change; it is corrected in `tests/test_skills_smoke.py`. After the correction that test alone was re-run
(`-k seeded -m live`) as each role and passed (1 passed). **The full suites were not re-run after the correction.**
The two end-to-end cases (ALERT-01 FILE, ALERT-16 NOT_FILE) are in the passing set in both roles. The audit-export test is skipped because the optional audit export is not provisioned.
Nothing was recorded to the ledger: those tests write inside a transaction and roll back, and assert that no row is left behind.
Local paths are replaced with <repo>, <tmp> and <scratch>; nothing else is changed.

